    764:| §C4 ATTACK_VECTORS — Anderson localisation Lyapunov exponent gamma(E) of chi_P-driven discrete 1D Schrödinger operator (cross-domain: Aizenman-Warzel random operators, Furstenberg-Kifer theorem) | FAIL | E | Frontier attack on whether chi_P deviates from random pseudorandomness on a SPECTRAL-GLOBAL statistic (Lyapunov exponent) — orthogonal to all 36 prior pseudorandomness measures (which are local correlation / entropy / Fourier / tensor rank / Gowers). Setup: H psi(n) = -psi(n+1) - psi(n-1) + V(n)psi(n), transfer matrix T_n = [[V(n)-E, -1],[1,0]] in SL(2,R), gamma(E) = lim (1/N) log ||T_N..T_1||. Pastur-Figotin perturbation for sparse V in {0,1}: gamma(E) ~ rho(1-rho)/(8 sin^2 k), E = -2 cos k in (-2, 2). Vectorised numerical Lyapunov estimator with periodic L^2 renormalisation, O(N) per energy. **Naive Bernoulli baseline at N=10^5, 50 seeds, 51 energies**: gamma_prime(E) deviates from gamma_bern_mean(E) by max |z| = 88.5 sigma at E = 0.108 (k = pi/2 parity resonance). Z-score grows as sqrt(N): 12.3 at N=10^4 → 88.5 at N=10^5. **Confounder: chi_P concentrated on odd indices.** Parity-matched controls C1 (random subset of odd indices size pi(N)-1 plus V(2)=1) and C3 (chi_P shuffled within odd indices) reduce deviation but still leave 33 sigma at E=1.088 ~ -2 cos(2pi/3) = +1, the **mod-3 resonance** (free transfer matrix rotates 2pi/3 per step, maximally couples to mod-3 periodic potentials; chi_P has mod-3 structure since primes >3 are +-1 mod 3). **W-trick cascade** (random potential supported on {n : gcd(n, W) = 1}, plus delta at small primes p|W): max |z| = 33 (W=2) → 12 (W=6) → 6.3 (W=30) → 6.1 (W=210) → 4.0 (W=2310, N=2*10^5). Cascade ends at residual ~ 4 sigma, borderline noise (Bonferroni 0.05/31 → z_thresh ≈ 3.16). **Same structural reason as E2.13/S85** (Gowers U^k of chi_P → Hardy-Littlewood singular series, recovered by W-trick): chi_P deviation is fully captured by small-modulus residue-class structure. Adds new EDGE E2.14: gamma(E) of Schrödinger operator with V=chi_P deviates from random Lyapunov by a quantity that W-tricks down to noise. **Closure mode E**: deviation IS the spectral signature of Hardy-Littlewood / Bombieri-Vinogradov equidistribution mod q; no additional spectral structure beyond what equidistribution already gives; algorithmic gamma extraction costs Theta(N), not polylog. **Cross-domain ingredient performed real work**: transfer-matrix product / Lyapunov machinery (Aizenman-Warzel 2015 *Random Operators*, Furstenberg-Kifer 1983) had never been applied to chi_P; the spectral signature of the W-trick at the Anderson-Lyapunov level is novel. **PROVIDES SECOND INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION** (after E2.13/S85) that chi_P structure = HL equidistribution mod q, in a category orthogonal to additive combinatorics. Cites E2.13, E1.10, E3.13, E7.1. Cross-domain refs: Aizenman-Warzel 2015 (AMS GSM 168); Furstenberg-Kifer 1983 Israel J. Math. 46; Pastur-Figotin 1992; Green-Tao arXiv:math/0606088 (W-trick). See experiments/dynamical/anderson_localisation_chi_p/anderson_localisation_chi_p_results.md. | 88 |
    770:| §G1 ATTACK_VECTORS — Liouville Anderson Lyapunov: spectral signature of Möbius pseudorandomness (cross-domain: Anderson localisation [reused S88] + Möbius/nilsequence orthogonality, Green-Tao 2012 *Annals* 175 = arXiv:0807.1736; Sarnak 2010 IAS lectures; Tao 2016 logarithmic-Chowla = arXiv:1509.05422) | FAIL | E | First wild-swing attack into the multiplicative regime beyond the W-trick wall. Setup identical to S88/E2.14 except potential is the **centered multiplicative encoding** V(n) = lambda(n) ∈ {-1, +1} (mean → 0 by PNT for Liouville, variance = 1 exactly, NOT the {0, 1} encoding S88 used). Pastur-Figotin prediction in-band collapses to gamma_PF(E) = 1/(8 sin^2 k), exactly matching i.i.d. Rademacher ±1 baseline. Question: any sustained |z| > 5 deviation gamma_lambda(E) - gamma_Rademacher(E) at any energy, NOT W-tricked away — would be A-grade Möbius-side spectral non-orthogonality. **Empirical at 51 energies in E ∈ [-2.95, 2.95], three sample sizes: max |z| = 1.78 (N=10^5, 50 seeds, argmax E=-0.236), 2.16 (N=3·10^5, 50 seeds, argmax +0.118), 2.04 (N=10^6, 100 seeds, argmax -2.006).** All below 51-energy Bonferroni threshold z = 3.16. Argmax energy WANDERS between runs (statistical, not arithmetic). chi^2 / K = 0.49-0.69 (Rademacher prediction = 1; lambda is sub-Rademacher). L^2 distance from Rademacher mean: lambda lies at empirical p ≈ {0.58, 0.86, 0.59} of the seed-to-seed Rademacher distribution. Pastur-Figotin agreement: gamma_lambda / gamma_PF = 0.9317 (std 0.32) inside band, identical to gamma_Rademacher_mean / gamma_PF = 0.9309 to 4 decimals. **Independent off-spectral check (two-point Chowla aggregate at N=10^6, h=1..16): Σ z_h^2 = 4.77 vs Rademacher chi^2_16 mean 16, std sqrt(32) ≈ 5.7** — empirical p ≈ 0.997, lambda is *more Rademacher-like than Rademacher* on Chowla. All 16 individual lag z's |z_h| ≤ 1.11. **Stark contrast with E2.14 (chi_P, S88) at same N=10^5 grid: chi_P max |z| = 88.5σ at locked E=0.108 (parity resonance), required W=2310 sieve to reduce to ~4σ; lambda needs no W-trick at all and |z| flat across two orders of N magnitude.** **Mechanism (structural reason for closure mode E):** Möbius/nilsequence orthogonality (Green-Tao 2012, arXiv:0807.1736) predicts lambda is asymptotically orthogonal to all nilsequences including periodic ones; Lyapunov exponent of det-1 transfer-matrix Markov chain on PSL(2,R) is determined by Furstenberg-Kifer measure, a non-abelian analogue of GT nilsequence framework. lambda's centered multiplicativity destroys the mod-q resonance that drives chi_P's 88σ deviation. Sub-Rademacher Chowla aggregate (Σ z² = 4.77 ≪ 16) is consistent with Tao 2016 logarithmic-Chowla theorem (arXiv:1509.05422). **First non-W-tricked spectral measurement** in the project's 38-measure pseudorandomness battery to land at noise floor without sieving. **Pairs with E2.14 to ISOLATE the source of chi_P's Anderson-Lyapunov deviation as exclusively HL singular-series mod-q resonance:** lambda is the canonical chi_P-twin (density 1/2, centered, multiplicative) without mod-q resonance, so it has no spectral signal. **Closes the intended polylog opening:** if lambda-Lyapunov had detectable structure, the explicit-formula μ-side Σ Li(x^ρ) μ_ρ could plausibly be partial-summed in polylog. lambda is featureless ⇒ explicit-formula Möbius side is irreducible at this measurement scale. **Adds EDGE E2.18**: gamma_lambda(E) ≈ gamma_Rademacher(E) within seed noise across [-3, 3], flat in N up to 10^6, no W-trick needed. **Cross-domain ingredient (Möbius/nilsequence orthogonality) performed real work**: first project use; status in CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md upgraded UNUSED → USED E. Cites E2.14, E2.13, E1.10, E3.13. Cross-domain refs: Aizenman-Warzel 2015 *Random Operators* AMS GSM 168; Furstenberg-Kifer 1983; Pastur-Figotin 1992; Green-Tao arXiv:0807.1736 (Möbius nilsequence orthogonality, primary); Sarnak 2010 IAS lectures (Möbius randomness conjecture); Tao 2016 Forum Math Pi 4 e8 = arXiv:1509.0542