    784:| §D30 ATTACK_VECTORS — Pollicott-Ruelle resonances of χ_P-weighted Gauss-map transfer operator: does L_{χ_P} f(x) = Σ_n χ_P(n) f(1/(x+n))/(x+n)² have an isolated arithmetic resonance encoding π(x), à la Mayer 1991 dynamical-determinant representation of ζ via the unweighted Gauss map? (cross-domain: Pollicott 1985 Inventiones 81 / Ruelle 1976 Inventiones 34 / Mayer 1991 Bull. AMS 25 transfer operator spectral theory; Baladi 2018 *Dynamical Zeta Functions* Springer Ergeb. 68) | FAIL | E | Frontier wild_swing S140 on the FIRST dynamical-spectral / transfer-operator measurement on χ_P, recommended next pick per S139 critique single-pick annotation. Chebyshev-Lobatto barycentric collocation on [0,1], (M_grid+1)-dim matrix; cylinder truncation n_max sweeping {100, 200, 400, 800}; 200 controls per ensemble at M=80, n=400; 5 baselines (B_naive=Bernoulli ρ, B_supp=cardinality-matched random subset of [2..n_max], B_par=parity-matched, B_cra=Cramér 1/log n, B_crao=Cramér+odd-parity most stringent); plus Rademacher controls for Liouville. **Pre-registered falsifiers**: F-A unweighted h=1 reproduces Mayer/GKW spectrum within 1e-3 (sanity); F-B B_crao closure within ±2σ (mode E); F-C ≥3σ deviation persisting under refinement (mode I); F-D closed-form polylog identity (A-grade). **Outcome: B-grade case (i) mode E — F-A passes, F-B holds, F-C/F-D fail.** F-A: top-3 unweighted eigenvalues at M=160, n=800 = (0.99820, -0.30293, +0.10064) vs published GKW (1.0000, -0.30366300289, +0.10088637) — agreement < 0.2% on top-3, sanity ✓. **χ_P spectrum (M=120, n=400)**: |λ_0|=0.35961, |λ_1|=0.05103, |λ_2|=0.00792, |λ_3|=0.00128, |λ_4|=0.00021 — alternating signs, geometric decay (gap |λ_1|/|λ_0|=0.142), parallel to GKW structure. **Refinement-stable**: top-5 eigenvalues vary by <1% CV across (M_grid, n_max) ∈ {30..160}×{100..800}, real Pollicott-Ruelle resonances (not spurious-discretisation). **Closed-form prediction**: leading eigenvector of L_h overlaps unweighted Gauss density g