    777:| §D22 ATTACK_VECTORS — Higher-order Hodge Laplacian L_1 spectrum of the coprimality flag complex K_N := \{σ ⊆ [2..N] : σ pairwise coprime\} (cross-domain: combinatorial Hodge Laplacian on simplicial complexes; Lim 2020 SIAM Review 62 = arXiv:1507.05379) | FAIL | E | Frontier wild_swing S126 on whether the higher-order (k≥1) Hodge Laplacian spectrum of an arithmetic flag complex carries circuit-complexity content invisible to L_0 (CLOSED 356/387/E7.12/E7.16). Build K_N from the coprimality graph G_N = ([2..N], gcd(i,j)=1); compute B_1 (edges→vertices), B_2 (triangles→edges), B_3 (tets→triangles); diagonalise L_1 = B_1^T B_1 + B_2 B_2^T (and L_2 where feasible) at N ∈ {8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64, 96, 128} with 5–30 ER-flag-complex matched-density controls per N. **Pre-stated targets**: A-grade = uniform `λ_2^{(1)} > c > 0` spectral gap distinct from ER + TC⁰-computable boundary. B-grade case (E) = spectra match within KS / β_k within 2σ. B-grade case (I) = β_1 deviates ≥ 3σ — Möbius singular-series fingerprint. **Outcome: B-grade structural negative-shape closure plus a sharp new empirical identity.** **F1 — Hodge KERNEL is deterministically trivial**: `β_0(K_N) = 1`, `β_k(K_N) = 0` for k ≥ 1 ∀ N ≥ 3. Mechanism: Bertrand's postulate guarantees a prime `p ∈ (N/2, N]`; every such prime is **universal** in G_N (gcd(p, v) = 1 for all v ≠ p ∈ [2, N]) ⇒ K_N is a cone, hence contractible. **F2 — `λ_max(L_1) = |V| = N − 1` exactly** to 1e-13 absolute residual at all 9 tested N; ER controls saturate at `p\|V| + O(\sqrt{|V|}) < |V|` (max ER λ_max(L_1) at N=64 = 51.7 < 63). **F3 — Multiplicity identity (main empirical theorem)**: `mult(λ_max(L_1, K_N) = |V|) = C(k+1, 2) = k(k+1)/2` where `k = π(N) - π(N/2)` is the Bertrand-prime count. Verified perfectly at all 9 tested N: (N, k, mult) = (8,2,3), (12,2,3), (16,2,3), (24,4,10), (32,5,15), (48,6,21), (64,7,28), (96,9,45), (128,13,91); empirical = predicted in every cell. Mechanism (sketch): K_N = Δ^{k-1} \ast F(H) where Δ^{k-1} is the (k-1)-simplex on Bertrand primes U and H = G_N − U; the Horak-Jost 2013 join-spectrum formula gives multiplicity = #(0-faces ∪ 1-faces of Δ^{k-1}) = k + C(k, 2) = C(k+1, 2). Full proof is a single-page exercise in Friedman / Horak-Jost machinery; we report empirically and conjecture the closed-form theorem. **F4 — L_1 mean shift = triple-coprime singular series**: trace identity gives mean(L_1, K_N) − mean(L_1, ER_p) = 3(T_cp − T_ER)/|E| with `T_cp / T_ER → ∏_p (1 − 3/p² + 2/p³) / (6/π²)³ ≈ 1.27628` as N→∞ (asymptotic = 1.27628; empirical ratios 1.241–1.273 across N = 32..128). Z[mean(L_1)] grows: 3.04σ → 4.40σ → 5.82σ → 9.48σ → **18.33σ at N = 128** (≈ √N scaling). KS distance grows 0.21 → 0.33; KS p-values from 1.9e-11 to < 1e-300. **Mechanism for closure mode E**: F1, F2, F3 all reduce to the Bertrand-prime universal-vertex join decomposition (classical); F4 reduces to the well-known triple-pairwise-coprime singular-series identity (E2.13-adjacent). The Hodge cross-domain import IS quantitatively new (first higher-order arithmetic-flag-complex spectrum), but the arithmetic content collapses to known number-theoretic identities. **Pre-stated A-target NOT met**: `λ_min(L_1)` Z-score is +5.5σ at N=48 but only +2.5σ at N=64 — non-monotone, not a uniform-in-N spectral gap. **Refines / cites**: distinct from CLOSED 356/387 (L_0 only — Ramanujan sums); distinct from E7.12/E7.16 (L_0 Cayley spectra); first L_k for k ≥ 1 quantitatively computed for an arithmetic flag complex. **Adds EDGE E7.17**: mult(λ_max(L_1, K_N) = N − 1) = (π(N) − π(N/2))(π(N) − π(N/2) + 1) / 2 (empirical 9-cell, conjecture sketch via Horak-Jost join-spectrum). Joins HL-detection family with a NEW saturation category: Hodge L_1 mean reduces to triple-coprime singular series; first higher-order arithmetic Hodge fingerprint. **Cross-domain ingredient (Lim 2020 / Friedman 1996 / Horak-Jost 2013 combinatorial Hodge Laplacian) performed real work**: first project quantitative use; CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES §1 row "Hodge / Laplacian on simplicial complexes (higher-order L_k, k ≥ 1)" promoted PROPOSED (D22) → USED E with edge E7.17. **Channelled mathematician**: Friedman (combinatorial Laplacians, simplicial-complex Betti via spectral methods). **Successors proposed (S126)**: D22.a higher Hodge Laplacian on the 2-skeleton at N^{1/2}-sieved coprimality flag complex (test if F3 multiplicity identity persists when small-prime hubs are removed); D22.b non-trivial β_2 / β_3 search by removing universal-Bertrand-prime vertices by hand to break the cone collapse; D22.c Hodge Laplacian of the chi_P-induced sub-flag-complex (only prime vertices) — orthogonal to coprimality angle. Cites E2.13, E2.14, E2.16, E2.17, E2.19, E7.12, E7.16. Cross-domain refs: Eckmann 1944 *Comment. Math. Helv.* 17, 240; Friedman 1996 *Algorithmica* 21, 331; Horak-Jost 2013 *Adv. Math.* 244, 303; Lim 2020 *SIAM Review* 62(3), 685 = arXiv:1507.05379; Goff 2009 *J. Algebraic Combin.* 30, 215 (join spectrum); Kahle 2009 *Discrete Math* 309, 1658; Kahle 2014 *Annals* 179, 1085. See experiments/topological/hodge_coprimality_flag/hodge_coprimality_flag_results.md. | 126 |
